# Gate G-R8 baseline (scripts/gates/dm-vendored-clock-log.sh; Phase 9 design §16.1 G-R8, RG-3,
# §22.8.10 point 4, §22.33). The compiled library code of every crate of `cargo tree -p ghost-client-dm
# -e normal --features jni-bridge` on aarch64-linux-android and x86_64-linux-android, with the features
# of the shipped `ghost-client-net`, merged over both triples. Kinds: [lib] linked into the library;
# [proc-macro] and [build-time] run only while compiling. Every site, directive and note line ends in
# its reason after two spaces and '#'. An entry the scan finds and this file lacks fails the gate
# (unjustified); an entry here the scan no longer finds fails it too (stale). Regenerate at a pin
# change with GHOST_G_R8_PRINT=1 and complete every '# UNJUSTIFIED' by review, never by copy.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-26 by the S0′ gate slice from S0′'s V-8 baseline (client-core/dm-spike/baseline/
# g-r8-baseline.txt, 2026-09-16, measured on the ghost-dm-probe graph): the production graph holds the
# same 39 sites, none added and none gone; the 112 crates, 143 directives and 2 notes are new lines,
# each reviewed here. vodozemac, hpke, matrix-pickle and every libcrux crate: no site.
#
# Extended 2026-09-26 at the integration (design §22.33 item 16, the evasion review of the S0′ gates):
# the scanner also lists the standard stream handles (`stdout`, `stderr`, `Stdout`, `Stderr`,
# `StdoutLock`, `StderrLock` — `writeln!(std::io::stderr(), …)` names no print macro) and the Unix
# socket types (`UnixStream`, `UnixListener`, `UnixDatagram` — `std::os::unix::net` is not `std::net`
# to a token scan). The production graph holds 4 such sites, all build-time, none linked: 43 in all.

# Sites (clock, logging, printing, network):
